    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! So I have this issue where if I reset a line hunk using gHH, it resets but puts the cursor at another line instead of the line where the hunk was reset. Is it possible to save the hunk line location and put the cursor back in the same line in any way.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-632+g33464189b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In a git tracked directory, if you reset hunk with gHH, the hunk resets but the cursor is put in a different line than the line where the hunk is located.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe cursor should be put in the same line after the hunk is reset.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe cursor is put in a random line after the hunk is reset.",
