            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`gHH` in fact consists from two parts: `gH` operator and `H` motion (see `:h H`). So it resets lines from current and up until the first visible (\"top\") line. As executing operator places cursor at the start of its target, cursor is moved to the top line.\r\n\r\nIf you want to resent current hunk, use `gHgh` (`gH` operator + `gh` textobject). If you want to reset current line, use `gH_` (`gH` operator + `_` textobject).",
